# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The Ubuntu base layer.
#
# One advisory in libbrotli-dev, fixed in a package version that cloudron/base has not shipped
# yet (6.0.1 is current, 2026-10-21). Not actionably fixable from this repository.
#
# Removal condition: the next cloudron/base bump.
CVE-2026-111497

# apt and libapt-pkg7.0, CVE-2026-109518 (remote code execution through hard link reuse during
# package download). The fix is in 3.2.1ubuntu0.1, which cloudron/base 6.0.1 does not carry; the
# base is built by Cloudron, not rebuilt here, and adding an apt upgrade to the Dockerfile would
# put the image on a package set no base tag describes.
#
# Exposure: the package manager runs at build time and inside `cloudron exec`, not on the
# request path. Worth fixing, not worth holding a release for.
#
# Removal condition: the next cloudron/base bump after the fix lands upstream.
CVE-2026-109518

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# npm, inside the Node runtime this package bundles (24.22.2).
#
# brace-expansion and undici ship in npm's own node_modules. The 1.0.6 release carried a Node
# bump (24.22.1 to 24.22.2) expecting it to clear them; it did not, and 24.22.2 is the newest
# release on the 24 line, so there is no bump to take. npm's dependencies are not ours to pin:
# repacking npm inside the image would diverge from the upstream Node artefact the Dockerfile
# consumes.
#
# Removal condition: the next Node 24.x release. Re-run the gate on the bump; if these persist,
# it is an upstream question, not a reason to keep the exception.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-109383
CVE-2026-109869
CVE-2026-19534
CVE-2026-87018
